//! What every file knows without an `import`: the types that the built-in members of a part
//! have. A name here is in scope everywhere, so a board writes `AssemblyMode::Hand` with no
//! import (ADR 0054).

/// Who puts a part on the board: the type of the built-in `.assembly` of every part, and of
/// the value a module offers for its parts (`.assembly_mode: AssemblyMode`, ADR 0042). It
/// decides the bill of materials, the placement file and the notes of `fab` (ADR 0024).
enum AssemblyMode {
    /// The board house places and solders the part: it is a line in the BOM and in the
    /// placement file, and it needs a supplier part number.
    Fab,
    /// Soldered by hand after the board comes back: it is in the fab notes, and on no BOM and
    /// no placement file.
    Hand,
    /// Not fitted at all: a mounting hole, a fiducial, a pad that a cable presses on. It is
    /// on no BOM and no placement file, and the fab notes list it as not fitted.
    None,
    /// The board house places and solders the part, and the owner ships the part to the board
    /// house: it is a line in the BOM and in the placement file, needs no supplier part number,
    /// and the fab notes list it as consigned (ADR 0084).
    Consigned,
}

/// The qualification a part claims, the type of the built-in `.qualification` of every part
/// and of the `.qualification` a board's `.environment` requires (ADR 0099). It is a family
/// and not a standard: AEC-Q100 (integrated circuits), AEC-Q101 (discrete semiconductors) and
/// AEC-Q200 (passives) are each `Aec`, and the `notes` of a catalog row say which of them its
/// datasheet states (Automotive Electronics Council, https://www.aecouncil.com/). A part's
/// qualification belongs to its ordering code and not to its kind: a part stands as qualified
/// only where a datasheet says so, and a row states nothing otherwise.
enum Qualification {
    /// The datasheet says the part is not qualified (the ordering code of the row is the
    /// commercial grade). As a requirement of an environment it asks for nothing.
    None,
    /// The datasheet says the part is qualified to an AEC standard of its kind.
    Aec,
}
